					// if directory, append /.envrc? Original: if directory name passed, treat as if /.envrc appended. How to detect directory? If path doesn't end with .envrc or .env? Actually exact can be dir or file. If it's a dir (exists and is dir?) or if it doesn't end with .envrc/.env? Let's check: man says "Each string can be a directory name or the full path to an .envrc file. If a directory name is passed, it will be treated as if it had been passed as itself with /.envrc appended."
					// So if path ends with .envrc or .env, keep as is, else append /.envrc. But what if path is like /tmp/bar (dir) vs /tmp/bar/.envrc (file)? We'll implement: if base is .envrc or .env, keep, else append /.envrc.
					base := filepath.Base(v)
